### Current UI Injection Capabilities

- **Delivery**: Shadow DOM element (`vi-ai-host`) injected into host page
- **Positioning**: Fixed bottom-right (for `body` target) or appended to specific selector
- **Types**: Popups, modals, floating widgets — all essentially the same pattern
- **Limits**: One injection at a time, per-intent caps (configurable)
- **Modes**: Pre-generated (fast, cached) or on-the-fly Gemini generation (dynamic, slower)
- **Close**: Built-in close button removes the element

---

## Current Limitations

1. **One-dimensional UX**: Everything is a popup/overlay — feels intrusive and easy to dismiss
2. **No persistence**: Closed elements are gone forever; no memory of what worked
3. **Static once injected**: UI doesn't react to continued behavior after injection
4. **No conversion tracking**: No feedback loop — system never learns if an injection converted
5. **Single injection at a time**: Can't compose multiple contextual nudges
6. **Body-only targeting**: Limited ability to inject *inline* within page content
7. **No A/B testing**: No way to compare injection strategies

